				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Cocoon auto-restart with exponential backoff and gRPC notification handlers\n\nAdd automatic restart capability for the Cocoon extension host sidecar. When the health monitor detects a crash, it schedules a restart with exponential backoff (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 seconds) up to 5 attempts via a new mpsc channel wired into CocoonProcessState.\n\nAlso add supplementary workspace activation events for well-known root config files (Cargo.toml, package.json, tsconfig.json, go.mod, pyproject.toml, CMakeLists.txt) that fire exact-filename activation events after the manifest-based phase, ensuring extensions activate even when the workspace opens after the initial scan.\n\nExtend the Vine gRPC notification dispatcher with four new handlers:\n- languageClient.status / languageServer.status — forwards language server status to Sky via Tauri event\n- extension.activating — logs extension activation for observability\n- task.completed / tasks.completed — removes task from active executions and emits completion to Sky\n- debug.session.stopped / debug.stopped — unregisters debug session and emits stop event to Sky\n\nImpact: Improves Cocoon resilience with self-healing restarts, closes activation gaps for workspace-root extensions, and wires language server, task, and debug lifecycle events from Cocoon to the Sky UI layer.",
			"SHA": "ac5b27c6a5931f91ea25c543529dbaa33e080743"
		}
	],
